From e27c985598870c271d87c94a03c2edc864622ccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:57:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): refuse a rotated work offset by name instead of
 posting it unrotated

The post stream carries only the offset's translation (OriginX/Y/Z), so a
G54 given a rotation (SetWcsOrigin, 3-2-1 alignment) posted world-axis
coordinates turned against the part, silently. The verification gate now
refuses every rotated offset a posted op uses, naming the setup, the
G-word, the angle and axis, and the operations. Offsets within 1e-9 rad
of identity post byte-identical to before. The slot law is shared by
wcs_context and the new clause.

Fixes #315

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
